  "body": "U5 of the tool library redesign (#3663). The tool editor of the tool library window gets a Recipes tab. The tab shows the speeds and feeds of a tool for each workpiece material.\n\nStacked on #3931 (U4). The commits of this PR only: https://github.com/qsmits/Camcraft/compare/9af86ad9f...issue/3896-tool-recipes-tab\n\nThe branch has the fixed U4 head `9af86ad9f` merged in (merge `b82b017bb`, no hand edits). That merge closes finding 1 of the review on `9a7f598b5` (the Apply holder refusal now judges the stored tool).\n\n## What changed\n- New tab \"Recipes\" between \"Tool\" and \"Details\" (`ToolEditorTab::Recipes`).\n- New `tool_library_dialog/recipes_tab.rs` (the tab) and `recipes_fill.rs` (the arithmetic). The tab calls the same cutting rows as Properties (`tool_cutting_rows::cutting_rows_with`). It does not copy them.\n- Read-only columns after each speed-and-feed row:\n  - surface speed `Vc = pi x D x n / 1000` (m/min, or sfm in an inch document);\n  - feed per tooth `fz = F / (n x z)` (mm, or inch);\n  - the mark \"document material\" on the row that the document material runs (`cutting::material_of`). When no row names that material, the mark is on the default (`Unknown`) row. With no material stated, no row has the mark.\n- \"Tool material\" and \"Flutes\" rows (draft fields). Suggest and fz need them, and the catalog tools state neither.\n- \"Suggest for <material>\" fills the row of that material in the window draft. The default material is the document material. The numbers come from `camcraft_app::cutting::compute`, which uses the pure table of `crates/tools/src/cutting.rs` (`WorkMaterial::window`, `rpm_for`, `feed_for`) and the stated limits of the document machine. It does not use `ApplyCuttingData`, because that command acts on an operation. A missing row is added. The stepdown and stepover of the row stay.\n- \"Copy from tool\" copies the plain material rows of another document tool into the draft. A row of the same material is replaced, and a new material is added. The default row, the recipes and the other rows of the draft stay.\n- \"Add material row\" is the existing button of the table.\n- Suggest and Copy write only the window draft and queue no command. The one Apply of the editor lands the draft as one `ChangeTool`: one undo step.\n- `tool_cutting_rows.rs` gets a small hook (`Extra`) for the extra cells. Its tests move to `tool_cutting_rows_tests.rs` (a `#[path]` module, no module-list change). The file goes from 324 to 225 lines.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3896-tool-recipes-tab.md`.\n\nCommands: `ChangeTool` only. No command is new, so no MCP tool is owed. MCP agents set the same rows with `edit_tool` (`cutting_data`).\n\nHeld back: \"the cutting group leaves the property summary\". U4 (#3931) held the Properties summary page back to #3930. Properties keeps its Cutting data group until #3930 lands the summary.\n\n## Readings\nEM-0600-4FL, carbide, 4 flutes, document material Aluminium 6061:\n- Unknown row 9500 rpm, 1800 mm/min: Vc 179 m/min, fz 0.047 mm.\n- Mild steel 6000 rpm, 1000 mm/min: Vc 113, fz 0.042.\n- Aluminium 6061 12000 rpm, 3000 mm/min: Vc 226, fz 0.062, marked \"document material\".\n- Suggest for Brass adds 11937 rpm, 1791 mm/min: Vc 225, fz 0.038. This is the middle of the carbide window of the table (Vc 225 m/min).\n\n## Pinning tests\nNew in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_library_recipes.rs`:\n- `suggest_fills_the_draft_and_apply_is_one_undo_step`: Suggest fills the window draft with the `cutting::compute` numbers and queues no command. Properties' draft of the same tool does not change. Apply is one undo step, and one undo restores the tool.\n- `copy_from_tool_copies_the_rows`\n- `the_document_material_row_is_marked`: the mark is on the Brass row, then on the default row (HDPE, no row), then on no row (no material). The Vc value of the row shows.\n\nNew unit tests in `recipes_fill.rs`: `surface_speed_and_feed_per_tooth_follow_the_handbook_relations`, `the_marked_row_falls_back_to_the_default_row`.\n\nUpdated: `page_layout_tool_library::layout_window_tool_editor`. The Recipes tab is between Tool and Details on the tab row. Its Suggest row is between the tabs and Apply.\n\nThe `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` goes from 1794 (U4 head) to 1799. No test is deleted. No snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Gate (Windows, winbuild, head b82b017bb merged with origin/main b13ebd440)\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 18 steps, 18 ok, 0 failed, 0 stalled, wall 6.1 min (ui build, ui lib, 16 ui suites). ui lib: 1621 passed, 0 failed, 8 ignored. It ran the pinning tests above and the two U4 tests of the review fix (`tool_library_assembly::the_refusal_judges_the_stored_tool_not_shorter_draft_flutes`, `tool_library_assembly::longer_draft_flutes_give_a_draft_note_not_an_apply_refusal`).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: exit 0.\n- The quick plan has 18 steps, not 10, because the diff against `origin/main` includes U4 (#3931).\n- No heavy step: this issue is P4, not P1. No post or toolpath changed, so no `example_catalog*` suite applies. The light lane was not run.\n- Earlier gate on head 9a7f598b5: 18 ok, wall 6.6 min.\n\n## Not exercised\n- A tool in an inch document: the sfm and inch columns are drawn, not pinned by a test.\n- Suggest against a machine with a stated spindle range or feed ceiling: the clamp is the code of `cutting::compute`, pinned by its own tests in app.\n- The window is 620 px wide by default. The table scrolls across in the window until the user makes the window wider.\n\n## Screenshots (headless, winbuild; the window made wider by a drag)\nBefore (U4 head 28fc33a2a): the editor has Tool and Details tabs only.\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3896/before-tool-tab.png)\n\nAfter: the Recipes tab with Vc, fz and the document material mark.\n![after recipes tab](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3896/after-recipes-tab.png)\n\nAfter: Suggest for Brass adds the Brass row to the draft.\n![after suggest](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3896/after-suggest-brass.png)\n\nChangelog: A Recipes tab shows a tool's speeds and feeds per material, with surface speed and feed per tooth, and can suggest or copy them.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #3896\n\n",
